You can create a custom WordPress block with a heading, paragraph, and image by following these steps:

1. Create a new PHP file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory of your WordPress installation. For example, `custom-block.php`.
2. In this file, add the following code to register the block:
```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Custom Block
Description: A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image.
*/

function register_custom_block() {
    wp_register_block_type(
        'custom-block/block',
        array(
            'title' => __( 'Custom Block' ),
            'description' => __( 'A custom block with a heading, paragraph, and image.' ),
            'render_callback' => 'render_custom_block',
        )
    );
}
add_action( 'init', 'register_custom_block' );
```
This code registers a new block type called `custom-block/block` with a title, description, and a render callback function `render_custom_block`.

3. Create a new PHP file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory to define the render callback function. For example, `custom-block-render.php`.
4. In this file, add the following code to define the render callback function:
```php
<?php
function render_custom_block( $attributes, $content, $block ) {
    $heading = $attributes['heading'];
    $paragraph = $attributes['paragraph'];
    $image_url = $attributes['image'];

    $image = wp_get_attachment_image( $image_url, 'full' );

    return sprintf(
        '<div class="custom-block">%s<h2>%s</h2><p>%s</p>%s</div>',
        $image,
        $heading,
        $paragraph,
        $content
    );
}
```
This code defines the render callback function `render_custom_block` which takes three arguments: `$attributes`, `$content`, and `$block`. It extracts the heading, paragraph, and image URL from the block attributes and uses them to render the block HTML.

5. In the `custom-block.php` file, add the following code to enqueue the block styles:
```php
function enqueue_custom_block_styles() {
    wp_enqueue_style( 'custom-block-styles', plugins_url( 'custom-block.css', __FILE__ ) );
}
add_action( 'enqueue_block_editor_assets', 'enqueue_custom_block_styles' );
```
This code enqueues a CSS file called `custom-block.css` which will be used to style the block.

6. Create a new CSS file in the `wp-content/plugins` directory to define the block styles. For example, `custom-block.css`.
7. In this file, add the following code to define the block styles:
```css
.custom-block {
